menu "ANCLA anchor"

config ANCLA_CAL_MODE
	bool "Antenna-delay calibration firmware"
	help
	  Build the calibration image instead of the production anchor.

	  main() hands the main thread to cal_run() rather than dispatching on
	  the configured mode, giving the board a `cal` console tree that lets
	  it act as a temporary SS-TWR initiator. Production images must never
	  enable this: a deployed anchor transmitting unsolicited polls would
	  collide with tag ranging traffic.

config ANCLA_RANGING_DEBUG
	bool "Ranging-path diagnostics"
	help
	  Compile in the DISCOVERY/WAVE responder verdict lines, the SLAVE
	  loop's RX heartbeat and frame counters, and raise the ranging
	  modules' per-module log levels to DBG.

	  Needed because those modules register at LOG_LEVEL_INF explicitly,
	  which hard-caps them no matter what CONFIG_LOG_DEFAULT_LEVEL says --
	  the beacon-guard suppression verdict in particular is a LOG_DBG that
	  a .conf overlay alone cannot reach. See src/uwb_debug.h.

	  Changes no frame, no timing constant and no gate, so a debug board
	  is a normal peer on air. It is still not a deployment image: the
	  per-frame logging and the heartbeat's extra SPI read both cost time
	  on the SLAVE loop.

config ANCLA_DEBUG_FORCE_HIGH_SEAT
	bool "Pre-fill low seat ids with dummy IDLE seats (bench-only)"
	default n
	help
	  Bench aid for measuring BLINK-slot arm jitter at a HIGH seat id with
	  only a handful of real tags on hand. gw_core assigns seat_id as the
	  first free index in seats[], so with 2-3 real tags every one of them
	  lands at seat_id 0, 1, 2.

	  NOTE the real ceiling: a fresh join's scan limit is
	  min(blink_n_slots, GW_MAX_SEATS), so seat_id can NEVER exceed
	  GW_MAX_SEATS-1 (127) even though BLINK_N_SLOTS is 134 -- the seats[]
	  array, not the blink schedule, is what caps this. Do not set
	  ANCLA_DEBUG_DUMMY_SEATS anywhere near 134; the highest seat_id this
	  can ever produce is 127, and the tag's known ms-rounding gap near
	  BLINK_N_SLOTS-1 (CLAUDE.md's Task 5 entry) is therefore structurally
	  unreachable on this build regardless of this option.

	  With this on, gw_core_debug_fill_seats() marks the first
	  ANCLA_DEBUG_DUMMY_SEATS entries of seats[] as occupied, IDLE-tier,
	  effectively-infinite-lease dummy seats before any real join happens
	  -- so the next real tag to join is pushed to seat_id
	  ANCLA_DEBUG_DUMMY_SEATS instead of 0. Off by default: it changes real
	  admission behaviour (fewer real seats available) and must never ship.

config ANCLA_DEBUG_DUMMY_SEATS
	int "Dummy seats to pre-fill"
	default 120
	depends on ANCLA_DEBUG_FORCE_HIGH_SEAT
	help
	  Must stay strictly below GW_MAX_SEATS (128) MINUS the number of real
	  tags you intend to join, or later real tags get refused admission
	  outright ("no free seat") instead of landing at a high seat id --
	  gw_core_debug_fill_seats() silently clamps to GW_MAX_SEATS-1 if you
	  set this at or above 128, which leaves only ONE free seat for every
	  real tag combined. 120 leaves 8 free seats (GW_MAX_SEATS-120), enough
	  headroom for a small bench fleet while still landing the first real
	  tag near the true seat_id ceiling of 127.

endmenu

source "Kconfig.zephyr"
